This time it took only 31 games  before ascending.
It seems that whenever I get past the mine I have 1:2 
chance of ascending. The other 1:2 is doing something horribly 
stupid like choking on food.

Decided to try conducts this time around. 
So ascended with no genocide, no polymorph, no selfpolymorph,
no el-word, almost no conflict. 

Beginning was not really eventful. Accidentally killed guards in
minetown. Converted the altar there. Was ready for the Quest by the time
I descended to it. 

Got +3 Sunsword from a monster (Some A, probably couatl) Nice light
source. It only blasted be once. Even though I dropped it once or twice.


A few YASD possilities and also YAAD.

Swam for a few turns on  no-teleport levels. (I had teleport and
teleport control from relatively early on). Moral of the story:
Don't move when confused and near water. In-game or otherwise.

Plane of Earth was as easy as I expected.
Plane of Air was easier than I anticipated. Steam vortices and energy
vortices make for great places to hide if you have the necessary
intrinsics. 
Plane of Fire was harder. 24 Archons for crying out loud!! 
Luckily I had a rubber chicken handy when 7 (seven) of them decided to
kill me all at the same time. 
I really hate the fact that they have shields of reflection by default.
I had a cursed scroll of gold detection but then
some fire giant decided to drop a boulder on the portal. 
I could have done this easier. I had holy water and an expired spell. 
I also had scrolls of charging and empty scrolls and magic markers.
Almost got slimed on Fire. A well timed prayer solved that problem.
Even though I was crowned Envoy of Balance.
Died once on Fire. I used conflict and something engulfed/swallowed me. 
(A fire vortex?) It then flew me over lava. Killed the thing. 
There I was, stuck in lava with no place to go. Tried to move. 
Leg is stuck, can't move. Put on ring of levitation. Still stuck.
Try to get out some more. Amulet saved me. The only AoLS that I saw
during the entire game. Then I used wand of cold
downward. Then miraculously I was free to fly where-ever I wanted. 
What happened to the lava that was holding my legs? (Bug?)
Water was quick. I just floated to the other end and was lucky to hit the
portal almost immediately. 
Elemental Plane was easy. Went right. Blinded Death with a camera. 
Killed some monsters priests and Angels. #offered and ascended.
Could have easily cleared the level. 

Only weapons wielded were quarterstaff, Magicbane and pick-axe.

